# **The name the server picks when it is told none**, which is the only thing
# this session is about: every other one is handed a PASLS_SCRATCH by the
# harness, so none of them can see it. The `.tmpdir` marker leaves the variable
# unset and gives the server an empty TMPDIR of its own; what is checked is the
# file left in it afterwards, and it must be `pasls-<the server's pid>.pas`.
#
# A name without the pid is what stood here until ADR-0242, and two servers on
# one machine then wrote each other's documents. The mutation is exactly that:
# take the number out of the name and this session is the one thing that fails.
#
# The document is deliberately correct, because the scratch file is written
# whether or not the compilation says anything -- and a session that also
# pinned a diagnostic would be pinning two things at once.

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"processId":null,"rootUri":null,"capabilities":{}}}

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didOpen","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/quiet.pas","languageId":"pascal","version":1,"text":"program quiet(output);\nbegin\n  writeln('quiet')\nend.\n"}}}

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"shutdown"}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"exit"}
